#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The Hijrah: a journey in stages"
msgstr "Hijrada: safar wejiyaal leh"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "English working draft; no final narration or translation approved"
msgstr "Qabyo-qoraal shaqo oo Ingiriisi ah; ma jiro sheeko ama turjumaad kama dambays ah oo la ansixiyay"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Connect preparations, the stay at Thawr, the onward journey, and arrival while distinguishing an illustration from its evidence."
msgstr "Isku xidh diyaargarowga, joogitaankii Thawr, sii wadista safarka, iyo imaatinka adigoo kala saaraya sawir-gacmeedka iyo caddaymihiisa."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#: src/lib/guide-provider.js
#, ai
msgid "How did the journey continue after the cave?"
msgstr "Sidee buu safarku u sii socday godka ka dib?"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#: src/lib/guide-provider.js
#, ai
msgid "Show the onward journey"
msgstr "Muuji sii wadista safarka"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Before the journey"
msgstr "Safarka ka hor"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "This chapter follows the Hijrah: the Prophet Muhammad’s ﷺ migration from Makkah to Madinah. We will follow a few connected stages, from preparations for departure to arrival in Madinah."
msgstr "Cutubkani waxa uu raacayaa Hijrada: socdaalkii Nebi Muxammad ﷺ ee uu uga guuray Makkah ilaa Madiinah. Waxaynu raaci doonaa dhawr weji oo isku xidhan, laga bilaabo u diyaargarowga bixitaanka ilaa imaatinka Madiinah."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Before the Prophet departed, some Muslims had already moved to Madinah. Abu Bakr was preparing to leave too, but waited to accompany him. This was part of a wider movement, not a departure in which everyone travelled together."
msgstr "Kahor intaanu Nebigu bixin, qaar ka mid ah muslimiinta ayaa mar hore u guuray Madiinah. Abu Bakar na waxa uu isu diyaarinayay inuu baxo, laakiin wuxuu sugayay inuu raaco. Tani waxay qayb ka ahayd dhaqdhaqaaq ballaadhan, ee ma ahayn bixitaan ay dadka oo dhami wada safreen."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Preparing to leave"
msgstr "U diyaargarowga bixitaanka"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "When permission to depart had been given, preparations were made for the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr. ‘Aishah’s account describes provisions packed in a bag. Asma, Abu Bakr’s daughter, used part of her waist-belt to tie its opening."
msgstr "Markii oggolaanshaha bixitaanka la bixiyay, waxaa loo diyaargaroobay Nebiga ﷺ iyo Abu Bakar. Warbixinta Caisha waxay sharraxaysaa sahay lagu riday boorso. Asma, oo ahayd gabadhii Abu Bakar, ayaa isticmaashay qayb ka mid ah dhex-xidhkeeda si ay ugu xidho afkeeda."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "They also hired a skilled guide, entrusted him with two riding animals, and arranged to meet him at Thawr after three nights. The arrangements for the onward journey were already being made."
msgstr "Waxa kale oo ay kaydsadeen hage xirfad leh, waxayna ku aamineen laba neef oo gaadiid ah, waxayna ku heshiiyeen inay kula kulmaan Thawr saddex habeen ka dib. Diyaar garowgii sii wadista safarka mar hore ayaa la sii waday."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#: src/content/timeline.js
#, ai
msgid "Three nights at Thawr"
msgstr "Saddex habeen oo Thawr ah"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "After the preparations, the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr sheltered in a cave on Mount Thawr. ‘Aishah’s account in Sahih al-Bukhari records that they stayed there for three nights. This was a stage within the journey, not its destination."
msgstr "Diyaargarowga ka dib, Nebiga ﷺ iyo Abu Bakar waxay gabaad ka dhigteen god ku yaal Buurta Thawr. Warbixinta Caisha ee Saxiix al-Bukhari waxay qoraysaa inay halkaas joogeen saddex habeen. Tani waxay ahayd weji ka mid ah safarka, ee ma ahayn meeshii loo socday."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "During the stay, ‘Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr brought news of plans against them. He came after darkness and left before daybreak, returning to Makkah. His contribution was information."
msgstr "Intii ay halkaas joogeen, Cabdullaahi ibn Abi Bakar waxa uu u keeni jiray wararka ku saabsan qorshayaasha ka dhanka ah. Waxa uu imaan jiray madowga ka dib, waxaanu bixi jiray waaberiga ka hor, isagoo ku laabanaya Makkah. Kaalintiisu waxay ahayd xog-keenis."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Abu Bakr’s own account brings us closer to the danger of discovery. He was concerned that they might be seen if someone looked down. The Prophet reassured him."
msgstr "Warbixinta Abu Bakar laftiisa ayaa inoo soo dhoweynaysa khatarta ah in la ogaado. Waxa uu ka walwalsanaa in la arki karo haddii qof hoos u eego. Nebiguna wuu u xaqiijiyay (oo dejiyay)."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The Quran also recalls the two in the cave and the reassurance given to the companion. Ibn Kathir’s commentary on the passage explains the reassurance through Allah’s help and support."
msgstr "Quraankuna wuxuu sidoo kale xusayaa labadii ku jiray godka iyo xaqiijintii la siiyay saaxiibka. Tafsiirka Ibn Kathir ee aayaddan wuxuu ku sharraxayaa xaqiijintaas gargaarka iyo taageerada Alle."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The journey continues"
msgstr "Safarku wuxuu sii socdaa"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The arranged meeting with the guide connects the stay at Thawr to the next stage. When the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr continued, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah and the guide went with them. The account says that the guide led them by the coastal way."
msgstr "Kulankii lagu heshiiyay ee hagaha wuxuu isku xidhayaa joogitaankii Thawr iyo wejiga xiga. Markii Nebiga ﷺ iyo Abu Bakar ay sii wadeen safarka, Caamir ibn Fuhayrah iyo hagaha ayaa raacay. Warbixintu waxay sheegaysaa in haguhu uu ku hoggaamiyay jidka xeebta."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "That description gives us part of the route’s character, but not every turn or stopping place. The connection shown here is schematic; it is not a measured itinerary."
msgstr "Sharaxaadkaasi wuxuu na siinayaa qayb ka mid ah dabeecadda jidka, laakiin maaha leexasho kasta ama meel kasta oo la istaago. Isku xidhka halkan lagu muujiyay waa mid guud; maaha khariidad cabbiran."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "Arrival and a new beginning"
msgstr "Imaatinka iyo bilow cusub"

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "In Madinah, Muslims went out to wait after hearing that the Prophet ﷺ had left Makkah. The arrival account describes their reception of him and his stay among Bani ‘Amr ibn ‘Awf."
msgstr "Madiinah dhexdeeda, Muslimiintu waxay u baxeen inay sugaan ka dib markay maqleen in Nebigu ﷺ ka baxay Makkah. Warbixinta imaatinka waxay sharraxaysaa soo dhawayntii ay u sameeyeen iyo joogitaankiisii dhexdiisa Bani Camr ibn Cawf."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "The account goes on to describe a date-drying yard that became the site of the Prophet’s mosque in Madinah. It records the Prophet carrying bricks with those building it."
msgstr "Warbixintu waxay sii sharraxaysaa meel timirta lagu qallajiyo oo noqotay goobtii masaajidka Nebiga ee Madiinah. Waxay qoraysaa in Nebigu uu lebenka la siday kuwii dhisayay."

#: src/content/first-chapter.js
#, ai
msgid "You followed preparations, a period of shelter, the onward journey, and arrival. You met different forms of help and read accounts of reassurance. This is a selected account, not a complete history of every episode or consequence of the Hijrah."
msgstr "Waxaad raacday diyaargarowgii, xilligii gabaadka, sii wadista safarka, iyo imaatinka. Waxaad la kulantay noocyo kala duwan oo gargaar ah waxaadna akhriday warbixinno xaqiijin ah. Tani waa warbixin la xushay, ee maaha taariikh dhammaystiran oo ku saabsan dhacdo kasta ama natiijada Hijrada."

